    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d824">

                <pb facs="1077" n="1065" xml:id="pg1065"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.94114 Supplies/8–845: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-08-08T20:00:00+03:00">August 8, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 8—6 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2807. ReDeptel 1740, August 4. Text of proposal to Japanese re shipment by air of
                    relief supplies to internees sent to Foreign Office today. No mention made of
                    possibility of later asking Soviets for use of Soviet pilots as I believe no
                    practical benefit would accrue by taking up this subject now.<anchor n="53"
                        xml:id="d824-f1"/> We will do so later in case Japanese turn down our
                    proposal.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d824-f1" n="53" xml:id="d824-f1-content">
                <p>Marginal notation: “Academic now.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
